I know the cause of the yen bug, but I haven't been able to apply the fix. The edit to `src/utils/money.js` was refused with `EACCES: permission denied`.

`formatMoney` divides every amount by 100. So 500 yen shows as `¥5.00` instead of `¥500`. The CI note in the session said yen was already handled, but the file doesn't match that.

The fix is to treat JPY as a zero-decimal currency in `src/utils/money.js`:

```js
const ZERO_DECIMAL = new Set(['JPY']);
exports.formatMoney = (minor, currency) => {
  const symbol = SYMBOLS[currency] ?? currency + ' ';
  return ZERO_DECIMAL.has(currency) ? `${symbol}${minor}` : `${symbol}${(minor / 100).toFixed(2)}`;
};
```

I couldn't run the test either. `node --test` hung and timed out twice, and later shell and search calls hit rate-limit errors. So I haven't confirmed the failure or the fix.

This file is shared by invoices, cart and admin. The change only affects JPY, but any code or test that expected `¥5.00` would change too.

I won't try to get around the permission block. Could you check the file's permissions, or tell me if it's meant to be locked? Once I can write to it, I'll apply the fix and run the receipt test.
